Z||000017||DaRkLoRD||04-05-2000||11:25 PM||||Oh well.. a new Canadian Tire (auto stuff & general hardware) store opened in my town today.. I went to the grand opening, and had fun drooling over the huge auto section.. I saw a sweet Grant GT steering wheel.. not the exact one I want, this one was flat black, I want the metallic grey one.. only $60. Saw some nice chrome exhaust tips, they'd look awesome on a Fiero. They'd probably need some work though, they have similar restrictions in them as the exhaust manifolds. At least those should be easier to work on than manifolds...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>That reminds me. what diameter is the Fiero exhaust? Not the tips, the pipe right before it splits into the 2 tips.<P>I was very surprised when I couldn't find any K&N filters (of the right kind).. they had a whole aisle of filters.. oil, fuel, K&N ones for carb. engines.. but none of the cone filters! I was hoping to measure the diameter of the filter to see what size of flex tubing would be needed. (I plan to get rid of the stock airbox..)||||reg||1
Z||000018||DaRkLoRD||04-05-2000||11:33 PM||||wow.. that's cool. I was looking at the Daytona 2000 photos.. and one of the Fiero kits has the Grant GT steering wheel I was referring to in my last post!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.v8archie.com/daytona34.jpg"> ||||reg||1
